  "manual_findings": [
    "Constructor borrows height slice only during call and owns outputVec. Capacity=floor(max(frame_width,advance)/advance).max(1) is estimate only; every input creates one column and empty input still returns capacity>=1/height0. Default layout capacity0 is a distinct value.",
    "Finite coordinates preserve negatives, nonfinite become0; dimensions clamp negatives/nonfinite0; invalid advance uses normalized column_width.max(1). Frame width and advance differ; leftx subtracts advance, so container fit/ink/rightedge alignment not guaranteed.",
    "The f64 right endpoint uses original normalized frame_x+frame_width. Every loop index independently computes exact right−(index+1)*advance. Original f32 right-overflow flag forces f64 recovery for every column, even finite candidate; it is not a running historical accumulator. Measured width count*advance finite-published, not geometric union or budget proof.",
    "UI owns upstream truncation and later y/height mutation, and may introduce other overflow beyond this helper. Values contain no borrowed input state; derives are standard, no custom traitimpl/dyn/registration/FFI in exact3.",
    "Five normal tests20 assertion sites plus one ignored bench are static declarations, zero executions. Fixed geometry, result-equivalence, source-shape predicate andMAX examples do not prove all floating inputs. Raw include_str splits firstcfg thenfirstfunction and evaluates3positive1negative string predicates; all4 remain statictrue, no benchmark assertion acceptance.",
    "Ignored benchmark16384heights/128checks/31pairs alternates ordering without warmup. Whole measure interval includes layout alloc/field consume/blackbox/drop/branch/loop; samples and sort/string/printing outside. Percentile ceil(n*p/100)-1 gives31p95index29, threshold candidatep95*100<=baselinep95*70. Printed2/1passes are constants and ignore label does not enforce profile/environment."
